ent which first of  all is not the most convincing accent in  the world but even beyond that I think  it would have played much better into  the feel of the film if he had just used  his normal speaking voice which if you  watch Family Guy's basically just Brian  the dog and I think that sort of because  his his normal speaking voice is like  the epitome of smug college-educated New  England looking down on people kind of  voice and I think that would have been  for what that character was is used that  would have been an even more cathartic  kind of character for him to be playing  than this weird not quite convincing  English accent he does there's also a  whole thing towards the end with Hilary  Swank that I'm not sure I needed to be  there I'm not sure what it added aside  from I guess about 15-20 minutes it  didn't it didn't like kill the movie or  anything I just seemed kind of oddly  obligatory it was a little weird but  overall it is it is a fun kind of  relaxed movie and it's playing with with  a different vibe from most sorts of  movies that you would expect from a high  so if you like heists but you maybe want  to try a different flavor if you like  you know these sorts of more country  sort of characters and and there there  is an interesting mix I mean I'm not  gonna say in there not stupid nub a  couple of them are stupid but some of  them are also really smart so it's not  over playing you know the dumb hillbilly  cliche or anything like that  and it feels respectful to to the  characters and their way of life to be  completely honest I say that as an  outsider looking in I'm not from the  south I don't a family in the south but  that's so take my opinion for what it's  worth probably not much but I I had fun  with this I get I don't want to oversell  it because it is slower pace over your  spectin like oh yeah it's a real romp of  ice it's not quite but it it it is fun  it is funny it's relaxed  it's kind of you know it feels like a  good palate clea